  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Maralal Resilience Livelihood Project(MRLP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Maralal Resilience livelihoods Project is  a 3 year project currently in its second year of implementation with annual funding from CAFOD with programme activities reviewed annually. The project will contribute to the CAFOD new programme strategy 2023-2030 with the overall goal of building Resilient communities in which people, particularly women and girls, thrive in a peaceful, well-governed, and healthy, supportive natural environment.
The project goal is to improve the food security of target vulnerable pastoralist communities through increased access to agricultural inputs, enhanced rangeland management and basic financial literacy skills.  which will be addressed through the following 3 interrelated outcomes;
Outcome 1: Capacities to mobilise resources and respond to climate shocks developed among target pastoralist communities.
Outcome 2: Enhanced community knowledge and skills on sustainable rangeland management
Outcome 3: Strengthened Learning, Collaboration and Coordination for knowledge/skills sharing and advocacy.

The project will be implemented in three subcounties of Samburu Central:Lodokejek and Suguta wards, Samburu North sub-county: Nachola, Ndoto wards and 
Samburu East: Uaso and Wamba North wards targeting 14,700 persons(8,000f, 6,700m).
The project shall work with already existing groups and community structures trough capacity strengthening activities and only form new groups where none are available.
The organization shall engage strategic partners to maximize impact and strengthen linkages and referrals. Caritas Maralal will work collaboratively with the county government and community structures in many aspects of implementation and most importantly, beneficiary identification.</narrative>
  </description>
